  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 6.2. Increased capacity of Member States to strengthen policies and strategies to promote and ensure equal opportunities, participation and treatment between women and men, including equal remuneration for work of equal value</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">On December 2021, the Montenegrin Bureau of Statistics (MONSTAT) released data on the Gender Pay Gap (GPG) for the first time since 2012. Between March and August 2023 the ILO shared its methodology to estimate the GPG and trained MONSTAT staff to use it and publish data on the GPG regularly. 
 
On 4 July 2023 the ILO organized a tripartite workshop to analyse the preliminary estimates and discuss policy options to address the Gender Pay Gap (GPG).

On 5 December 2023 the ILO supported the launch event where the new data was released.</narrative>
   </description>
